From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:56:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: start a load-only pass's encoder after its
 draw's compute

Zink ends its render pass for every barrier and begins another, and a
GPU particle simulation, which steps its particles by transform feedback
with the rasterizer discarded, has a pass for every step. A transform
feedback draw runs compute (the vertex stage, the counter kernel) and
then a render draw that makes the capture. The compute was recorded once
the pass's render encoder had started, so it took a command buffer of
its own that had to run before the render encoder, and the pass was
split to put it there: each step opened a main command buffer, with the
first render encoder of a command buffer taking about 2.5 MiB of
allocator storage, and a compute command buffer. Sling Shot's first
frames record as many as 523 such passes in one recording, 1.3 GiB of
command storage.

A pass whose attachments are all loaded (a load and a store of an
attachment nothing was drawn into leave it as it was; no clear, resolve,
layer, view mask, fragment shading rate attachment, secondary command
buffer contents or flag other than local read access control) now starts
its render encoder at its first draw, whether or not the draw
rasterizes, or at its first clear or render-stage timestamp. A transform
feedback draw in such a pass flushes its state to no encoder, records
its compute in the main command buffer in order, then starts the encoder
and flushes the state again before the render draw, as it would have
been drawn. The counter copies around a capture stop the encoder of such
a pass and run in the main command buffer too, and the pass's next draw
starts another that loads what the first stored. A pass that ends
without an encoder leaves its compute encoder open, so the barrier
between two passes is the intra-encoder barrier it already is. The
passes of a recording then share one main command buffer.

Command storage is still linear in the passes. An encoder costs storage
whichever command buffer holds it: a chain of 129 passes takes 3 command
buffers, 131 render and 133 compute encoders and 84 MiB at the end of
the recording, about 0.65 MiB a pass, where the canonical driver takes
518 command buffers and 656 MiB. What goes is the first-encoder cost of
every command buffer and the compute command buffers of the splits, not
the growth.

A draw that reserves from the geometry heap before its pass's encoder
starts (an unroll, an indirect capture's setup) pins the heap with no
encoder open, so its reset is recorded ahead of its reservations, and
starting the encoder begins a new segment: nothing would reset what the
draw reserved, and the next draw to reserve counted its demand from zero
on a heap that was not empty and could be refused, dropping its
geometry. The draw's segment now carries across the start: the heap is
pinned again with the encoder open, which queues the reset after the
pass, and the demand is kept. That leaves a post-render command buffer
open, so the pass cannot pause its encoder again, and a chain of such
passes does not share a main command buffer: 25 passes of indexed or
indirect captures take 53 command buffers and 69 MiB, where the
canonical driver takes 102 and 130 MiB. A direct capture writes its
records to the pool and no longer pins the heap, which queued a reset
after every pass of that kind, deferred or not.

Nothing rendered or captured changes. A pass that clears, resolves, has
layers, secondary command buffer contents or no attachments starts its
encoder when it begins, as before. The sample count an encoder started
late has comes from the pass's attachments. A failed recording that has
no encoder behaves as it does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c |  55 ++++++++-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h |  21 +++-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c   | 154 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c |   6 +
 4 files changed, 223 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
index 8390f70828acc23163e8924530cde655bb20980a..879e025d420c124a071127f216cad569a1400fa2 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -457,10 +457,18 @@ cs_get_render(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
 {
    struct kk_graphics_state *gfx = &cmd->state.gfx;
 
-   if (gfx->need_to_start_render_pass) {
-      gfx->render.samples = gfx->pipeline_sample_count;
-      mtl_render_pass_descriptor_set_default_raster_sample_count(
-         cmd->state.gfx.render_pass_descriptor, gfx->render.samples);
+   /* A draw that launches compute first leaves the pass unstarted until the
+    * compute is recorded, and its state goes to no encoder; see kk_draw. */
+   if (gfx->need_to_start_render_pass && !gfx->launch_before_encoder) {
+      /* A pass with attachments gives its descriptor the sample count they
+       * have, which holds for every encoder it starts. A pipeline's count
+       * stands for a pass that has no attachment to say. */
+      if (!gfx->render.load_only) {
+         gfx->render.samples = gfx->pipeline_sample_count;
+         mtl_render_pass_descriptor_set_default_raster_sample_count(
+            cmd->state.gfx.render_pass_descriptor, gfx->render.samples);
+      }
+      gfx->render.deferred_start = false;
       gfx->need_to_start_render_pass = false;
       cs_start_render(cmd);
    }
@@ -644,6 +652,45 @@ cs_end(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
    }
 }
 
+/* Ends a render pass's encoders. A pass that has no render encoder at its end
+ * ends without closing the compute encoder it recorded into the main command
+ * buffer, so that the passes of a transform feedback chain, which Zink ends
+ * for every barrier between them, share one main command buffer and one
+ * compute encoder between render encoders: a barrier there is an
+ * intra-encoder barrier, and the next render encoder to start closes it.
+ * Resolves and publications the encoder owes close with it, as at the end of
+ * any pass. */
+void
+cs_end_render_pass(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   if (cmd->state.gfx.render.deferred_start && cmd->gfx.encoder == NULL &&
+       cmd->post_gfx->encoder == NULL &&
+       util_dynarray_num_elements(&cmd->pre_gfx->ts_resolves,
+                                  struct kk_ts_resolve) == 0)
+      return;
+
+   cs_end(cmd);
+}
+
+/* Stops the render encoder of a pass that only loads its attachments, so that
+ * the compute recorded next runs in order in the main command buffer rather
+ * than in a command buffer of its own that precedes the encoder and splits
+ * the pass. The pass's next draw starts an encoder that loads what this one
+ * stored. */
+void
+cs_pause_render(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   struct kk_graphics_state *gfx = &cmd->state.gfx;
+
+   if (!gfx->render.load_only || cmd->gfx.encoder == NULL ||
+       cmd->pre_gfx->encoder != NULL || cmd->post_gfx->encoder != NULL)
+      return;
+
+   kk_stop_encoder(cmd, &cmd->gfx);
+   gfx->render.deferred_start = true;
+   gfx->need_to_start_render_pass = true;
+}
+
 /* Closes every encoder and command buffer, in submission order. */
 void
 cs_flush(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
index 65aa82c7d8b0798c393a709f5fa5a1f0485543a4..28d9eea8e7870326547b987455c502f85b55d7b9 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -186,6 +186,16 @@ struct kk_rendering_state {
    struct kk_attachment stencil_att;
    struct kk_attachment fsr_att;
 
+   /* The pass has attachments and began with every one of them loaded and
+    * nothing else to do (see kk_rendering_defers_encoder), so its Metal
+    * render encoder can start late and stop early: nothing is lost when it
+    * does not exist, and the next one picks the pass up where it was. */
+   bool load_only;
+   /* A load-only pass has no render encoder now. Its next draw, whether or
+    * not it rasterizes, its next clear and its next render-stage timestamp
+    * start one. */
+   bool deferred_start;
+
    uint32_t bresenham_samples;
    bool sample_locations_enable;
    uint32_t sample_locations_count;
@@ -214,6 +224,11 @@ struct kk_graphics_state {
    bool is_cull_front_and_back;
    bool need_to_start_render_pass;
 
+   /* The draw being recorded runs compute before its render draw and its
+    * pass has no render encoder yet: the encoder starts after that compute,
+    * so flushing the draw's state until then must not start one. */
+   bool launch_before_encoder;
+
    /* Set while a draw records the work that follows flushing its state into
     * the render encoder. A render pass split then flushes that state into
     * the encoder that resumes the pass. */
@@ -483,6 +498,8 @@ void kk_cmd_buffer_set_vertex_amplification(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
 mtl_compute_encoder *cs_get_compute(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, bool pre_gfx);
 void cs_stop_pre_compute(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
 void cs_end(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
+void cs_end_render_pass(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
+void cs_pause_render(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
 void cs_flush(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
 /* Re-emits the graphics state of the draw being recorded into a render
  * encoder that restarted after the draw flushed it. */
@@ -500,7 +517,9 @@ kk_cmd_buffer_dirty_all_gfx(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
    cmd->state.gfx.descriptors.root_dirty = true;
 
    /* The segment's heap reset is queued. A draw that needs the heap again
-    * pins it for the new segment and queues another. */
+    * pins it for the new segment and queues another. A draw that reserved
+    * from the heap before its pass's encoder started is the exception: it
+    * carries its segment across the start (kk_start_render_after_launch). */
    cmd->heap_in_segment = false;
    cmd->heap_demand_B = 0;
 }
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
index 5dfe1450cc5e11991466b90770f2582c7eb7f658..d0f8a163cb2d04f70138fce089373f6b33f139ef 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
@@ -347,6 +347,61 @@ kk_pipeline_attachment_mask(const struct kk_shader *vs)
    return mask;
 }
 
+/* Whether an attachment is left as it is: nothing in it is cleared, and
+ * nothing is resolved out of it. */
+static bool
+kk_attachment_is_loaded_only(const VkRenderingAttachmentInfo *info)
+{
+   return info == NULL || info->imageView == VK_NULL_HANDLE ||
+          (info->loadOp == VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_LOAD &&
+           info->resolveMode == VK_RESOLVE_MODE_NONE);
+}
+
+/* Whether a pass may start its Metal render encoder at its first draw instead
+ * of when it begins, and stop it for compute that follows a draw.
+ *
+ * A pass that only loads its attachments does nothing to them until a draw
+ * is recorded: the load and the store of an attachment that nothing was
+ * drawn into leave it as it was, so an encoder that holds no draw is not
+ * needed, and one that stops loads again what it stored when the next
+ * starts. Zink ends the pass of every transform feedback draw for its
+ * barriers and begins another, and a draw of that kind runs compute before
+ * its render draw. The compute is recorded in the main command buffer, in
+ * order, only while the pass has no encoder; once one has started, compute
+ * takes a command buffer of its own (see cs_get_compute), and a render
+ * encoder that starts a command buffer costs it megabytes of allocator
+ * storage (see cs_start_render).
+ *
+ * Every other pass starts its encoder at once. A clear, a resolve, layers, a
+ * view mask or a flag that suspends, resumes or resolves in a custom way
+ * acts on the attachments or on how the encoder begins, and a fragment
+ * shading rate attachment is bound to it. The only flag a plain pass may
+ * carry is local read access control, which only restricts the order of a
+ * draw's accesses. */
+static bool
+kk_rendering_defers_encoder(const VkRenderingInfo *info)
+{
+   if ((info->flags &
+        ~(VkRenderingFlags)
+           VK_RENDERING_LOCAL_READ_CONCURRENT_ACCESS_CONTROL_BIT_KHR) != 0u ||
+       info->viewMask != 0u || info->layerCount != 1u)
+      return false;
+
+   const VkRenderingFragmentShadingRateAttachmentInfoKHR *fsr =
+      vk_find_struct_const(info->pNext,
+                           RENDERING_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_ATTACHMENT_INFO_KHR);
+   if (fsr != NULL && fsr->imageView != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
+      return false;
+
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < info->colorAttachmentCount; i++) {
+      if (!kk_attachment_is_loaded_only(&info->pColorAttachments[i]))
+         return false;
+   }
+
+   return kk_attachment_is_loaded_only(info->pDepthAttachment) &&
+          kk_attachment_is_loaded_only(info->pStencilAttachment);
+}
+
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
 kk_CmdBeginRendering(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
                      const VkRenderingInfo *pRenderingInfo)
@@ -499,9 +554,14 @@ kk_CmdBeginRendering(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
    // it
 
    /* Rendering with no attachments requires pushing the start of the render
-    * pass to first pipeline binding to know sample count. */
+    * pass to first pipeline binding to know sample count. A pass that only
+    * loads its attachments starts at its first draw, clear or render-stage
+    * timestamp, whether or not the draw rasterizes; its descriptor, which
+    * loads every attachment, is complete now. */
+   const bool deferred =
+      !no_framebuffer && kk_rendering_defers_encoder(pRenderingInfo);
    cmd->state.gfx.render_pass_descriptor = pass_descriptor;
-   if (!no_framebuffer)
+   if (!no_framebuffer && !deferred)
       cs_start_render(cmd);
 
    /* Metal consumes the initial load actions when the encoder starts. Keep a
@@ -510,7 +570,9 @@ kk_CmdBeginRendering(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
                             render->bound_attachments, true);
    kk_set_depth_stencil_attachments(pass_descriptor, render,
                                     render->bound_attachments, true);
-   cmd->state.gfx.need_to_start_render_pass = no_framebuffer;
+   cmd->state.gfx.need_to_start_render_pass = no_framebuffer || deferred;
+   render->load_only = deferred;
+   render->deferred_start = deferred;
 
    kk_cmd_buffer_dirty_all_gfx(cmd);
 
@@ -649,7 +711,7 @@ kk_CmdEndRendering2KHR(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
    };
 
    /* Clean up previous encoder */
-   cs_end(cmd);
+   cs_end_render_pass(cmd);
    mtl_release(cmd->state.gfx.render_pass_descriptor);
    cmd->state.gfx.render_pass_descriptor = NULL;
 
@@ -3844,6 +3906,31 @@ kk_tess_heap_bound(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, const struct kk_draw_data *draw)
           align64(patches * points * 8u, 16);
 }
 
+/* Starts the encoder of a pass whose draw has recorded its compute. The
+ * start begins a new heap segment, but a draw that reserved from the heap
+ * (an unroll, an indirect setup) did so before it, and the render draw that
+ * follows reads what it reserved. The draw's segment therefore carries on
+ * into the encoder: it is pinned again with the encoder open, so that its
+ * reset is queued after the render segment, and the next draw to reserve
+ * counts its demand beside the draw's own. The reset the draw's pin queued
+ * ahead of its reservations stays, and frees what the segment before left. */
+static void
+kk_start_render_after_launch(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   const bool heap_in_segment = cmd->heap_in_segment;
+   const uint64_t heap_demand_B = cmd->heap_demand_B;
+
+   cs_get_render(cmd);
+
+   if (!heap_in_segment)
+      return;
+
+   cmd->heap_in_segment = true;
+   cmd->heap_demand_B = heap_demand_B;
+   libkk_heap_reset(cmd, kk_grid_1d(1), !cmd->gfx.encoder,
+                    cmd->heap->bo->gpu);
+}
+
 static void
 kk_draw_flushed(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
 {
@@ -3906,10 +3993,13 @@ kk_draw_flushed(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
       fprintf(stderr,
               "KK_UNROLL unrolled=%u provoking_rewrite=%u provoking_last=%u\n",
               requires_unroll, rewrite_direct_provoking, provoking_last);
-   /* Every stage the driver emulates, and every unroll, allocates from the
-    * device heap. */
+   /* Every unroll and every stage the driver emulates, other than transform
+    * feedback, allocates from the device heap. A direct draw that captures
+    * transform feedback writes its records to the pool, and an indirect one
+    * pins the heap where its setup reserves, as does an unroll above; pinning
+    * it here for the rest queued a heap reset, in a command buffer of its own
+    * after the pass, for every pass. */
    const bool needs_heap = requires_unroll || tess || emulate_geometry ||
-                           emulate_transform_feedback ||
                            emulate_line_raster || emulate_polygon_points ||
                            materialize_line_raster;
    if (requires_unroll) {
@@ -4013,10 +4103,48 @@ kk_draw_flushed(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
           is_polygon_primitive(raster_prim))
          draw_data.primitive_type = MTL_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_POINT;
 
+      /* The compute is recorded: the pass's encoder starts after it, and
+       * receives the draw's state flushed again. */
+      if (cmd->state.gfx.launch_before_encoder) {
+         cmd->state.gfx.launch_before_encoder = false;
+         kk_start_render_after_launch(cmd);
+         kk_flush_gfx_state(cmd);
+      }
+
       kk_dispatch_draw(cmd, draw_data);
    }
 }
 
+/* Whether the draw about to be recorded runs compute before its render draw,
+ * and its pass has no render encoder.
+ *
+ * A draw whose vertex stage the driver runs as compute to capture transform
+ * feedback records its capture in the render draw that follows, and the
+ * compute is recorded in the main command buffer, in order, when no render
+ * encoder is open. The pass's encoder therefore starts after the compute, so
+ * that the passes of a recording share one main command buffer instead of
+ * each ending one for the compute that followed its encoder's start.
+ *
+ * The emulated stages that follow vertex capture are left out: tessellation,
+ * the geometry shader, and the line and polygon-point rasterizers each
+ * produce compute of their own around the render draw. */
+static bool
+kk_draw_launches_before_encoder(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   const struct kk_graphics_state *gfx = &cmd->state.gfx;
+   const struct kk_shader *vs = cmd->state.shaders[MESA_SHADER_VERTEX];
+
+   if (!gfx->render.deferred_start || !gfx->need_to_start_render_pass ||
+       cmd->gfx.encoder != NULL)
+      return false;
+
+   return vs != NULL && vs->info.vs.transform_feedback_emulation &&
+          !vs->info.vs.geometry_shader_emulation &&
+          !vs->info.vs.line_raster_emulation &&
+          !vs->info.vs.polygon_point_emulation &&
+          cmd->state.shaders[MESA_SHADER_TESS_EVAL] == NULL;
+}
+
 static void
 kk_draw(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
 {
@@ -4030,11 +4158,17 @@ kk_draw(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
 
    kk_cmd_select_line_raster_variant(cmd);
    data->upload_mask = build_per_draw_upload_mask(cmd);
+
+   /* The state of such a draw is flushed to no encoder for the compute to
+    * read: the encoder that starts after it marks all of it dirty and
+    * receives it again before the render draw. */
+   cmd->state.gfx.launch_before_encoder = kk_draw_launches_before_encoder(cmd);
    kk_flush_gfx_state(cmd);
 
    cmd->state.gfx.draw_state_flushed = true;
    kk_draw_flushed(cmd, data);
    cmd->state.gfx.draw_state_flushed = false;
+   cmd->state.gfx.launch_before_encoder = false;
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
@@ -4398,8 +4532,12 @@ kk_begin_end_transform_feedback(
    gfx->xfb.enabled = begin;
    if (copies) {
       struct kk_ptr copy_gpu = kk_pool_upload(cmd, &copy, sizeof(copy), 8);
-      if (copy_gpu.gpu)
+      if (copy_gpu.gpu) {
+         /* The copy reads what compute before the draw counted, so it may run
+          * between the pass's encoders, in order. */
+         cs_pause_render(cmd);
          libkk_copy_xfb_counters(cmd, kk_grid_1d(copies), true, copy_gpu.gpu);
+      }
    }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
index 6fb8e2b78ae7896e19d4dab89ee88ec17fd8e203..f230edd85d6bde1e2cf29e5dd1e5f566dd7d3707 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
@@ -390,6 +390,12 @@ kk_CmdWriteTimestamp2(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
       .availability_count = count,
    };
 
+   /* The sample of a render stage belongs to the pass's render encoder. A
+    * pass that has not started one starts it for the sample, as the encoder
+    * it would have begun with. */
+   if (mtl_stage && cmd->state.gfx.render.deferred_start)
+      cs_get_render(cmd);
+
    /* non-gfx or not found*/
    if (cmd->gfx.encoder && mtl_stage) {
       /* Metal permits a single timestamp sample for each render stage in an
